  "id": "Compound::DB04878 - Gene::8972",
  "verbalization": "Voglibose is implicated in the interaction with Si, which is involved in glucosidase activity, and this activity is linked to Mgam. The evidence suggests that Voglibose binds to Si, which then participates in glucosidase activity, ultimately being participated by Mgam. The varying specificity of the glucosidase activity (Alpha-1,4 vs. Alpha-glucosidase) does not alter the core mechanism, as all are forms of glucosidase activity. The final scores from the paths indicate a consistent relationship, suggesting that Voglibose's effect on Si leads to a shared participation in glucosidase activity, which in turn is associated with Mgam. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Voglibose influences Mgam through its interaction with Si and subsequent enzymatic activity.",
